  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN236.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">āṟṟāmai vāyilākappukka talaimakaṉ nīkkattukkaṭ pukka tōḻikkut talaimakaḷ colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said to the confidante, who had entered during the absence of HIM, who had entered with [his own?] lack of strength as a mediator.(?)</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN236.1">
        <l>maṇimaruṇ malara muḷḷi yamaṉṟa</l>
        <l>tuṇinī rilañcik koṇṭa perumī</l>
        <l>ṉariniṟak koḻuṅkuṟai vevviḷar mānti</l>
        <l>veṇṇe lariñar peynilai piṉṟai</l>
        <l>yiṭaṉila neritaru neṭuṅkatirp palcūṭṭup</l>
        <l>paṉipaṭu kāyppuṟam parippak kaḻaṉik</l>
        <l>karuṅkōṭṭu māat talaṅkuciṉaip putuppū</l>
        <l>mayaṅkumaḻait tuvalaiyiṟ ṟāa mūraṉ</l>
        <l>kāmam perumai yaṟiyē ṉaṉṟu</l>
        <l>muyntaṉeṉ vā<supplied>ḻi</supplied> tōḻi yalka</l>
        <l>laṇikiḷar cānti ṉampaṭ ṭimaippak</l>
        <l>koṭuṅkuḻai makaḷiri ṉoṭuṅkiya virukkai</l>
        <l>yaṟiyā maiyi ṉaḻinta <supplied>ne</supplied>ñci</l>
        <l>ṉēṟṟiya leḻiṉaṭaip polinta moympiṟ</l>
        <l>ṟōṭṭiruñ curiyaṉ maṇanta <supplied>mucciyi</supplied></l>
        <l><supplied>ṉāṭṭa</supplied> ṉattik kāṇi rōveṉa</l>
        <l>nāṭṭi ṉāṭṭi ṉūri ṉūriṟ</l>
        <l>kaṭalkoṇ ṭaṉṟeṉap puṉaloḻit taṉaveṉak</l>
        <l>kaluḻnta kaṇṇaḷ kātalaṟ keṭutta</l>
        <l>vāti manti pōla</l>
        <l>vētañ collip pētuperi tuṟavē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="8d">The man from a village,</l>
        <l>where the swaying twigs of the black-branched mango tree</l>
        <l corresp="7-8c">spread new flowers in the drops of diffuse rain</l>
        <l corresp="6">near the paddy fields, when the parched surface as dew falls is spread over</l>
        <l corresp="5">with the adornment of many long ears that are crushed on the ground of the place</l>
        <l corresp="4">after the rainy stage by the cutters of white paddy,</l>
        <l corresp="3">after they fed on the hot whiteness of beautiful-coloured fat pieces</l>
        <l corresp="2">from the big fish that was taken in the tank with clear water</l>
        <l corresp="1">overgrown with Muḷḷi, [its] blossoms like sapphires,</l>
        <l corresp="9">the greatness of [my] passion [for him] I did not know well;</l>
        <l corresp="10">I escaped at night, oh friend,</l>
        <l corresp="21">– in order to experience great folly, talking of [my] suffering,</l>
        <l corresp="20">like Ātimanti,</l>
        <l corresp="13">with a heart that was desolate because it did not know</l>
        <l corresp="12">a position to calm down in, like [other] women with curved earrings,</l>
        <l corresp="11">as [their] pretty silk clothes sparkle with decorative shining sandal,</l>
        <l corresp="19">[she] whose lover was lost , her eyes dimming,</l>
        <l corresp="18">saying “the sea has taken [him], the floods have cast [him] off”</l>
        <l corresp="17">[and], in land after land, in village after village:</l>
        <l corresp="16">“did you not see Āttaṉ Atti,</l>
        <l corresp="15">[his] tuft united with dark curls in a mass,</l>
        <l corresp="14">of flourishing valour, with a graceful gait the nature of a bull’s?”</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

